---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import TravelOptions from '../components/TravelOptions.astro';
import { toCity, toCampus } from '../data/travel';

const tba = ['Accommodation', 'Registration', 'Visa'];
const place = encodeURIComponent('Facultade de Informática, Campus de Elviña, A Coruña');
---

<Layout
  title="Attending · ESSIR 2027"
  description="Practical information for attending ESSIR 2027, 12 to 16 July 2027, A Coruña, Spain."
  page="attending"
>
  <PageHeader eyebrow="Practical information" title="Attending" />

  <div class="container">
    <div class="rows">
      <section class="row">
        <h2>A Coruña</h2>
        <div class="wide">
          <p>A Coruña is a port city of about 250,000 people on the Atlantic coast of <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Galicia_(Spain)">Galicia</a>, in north-west Spain. Most of it sits on a narrow peninsula, so the sea is never far: the <a href="https://www.coruna.gal/tourism/en/what-to-do-in-a-coruna/nature-and-sports">seafront promenade</a> runs for more than 12 km around the city, past the port and the two city beaches, Riazor and Orzán.</p>
          <p>Its best-known landmark is the <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tower_of_Hercules">Torre de Hércules</a>, a Roman lighthouse from the first century AD. It was restored in the 18th century, still works today and has been a <a href="https://whc.unesco.org/en/list/1312/">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a> since 2009. Along the harbour, the white glazed galleries of the Avenida da Mariña gave A Coruña its nickname, the city of glass. Behind them, the <a href="https://www.coruna.gal/tourism/en/what-to-do-in-a-coruna/art-and-culture">old town</a> has narrow stone streets, Romanesque churches and the Praza de María Pita, named after <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mar%C3%ADa_Pita">the woman</a> who led the defence of the city against an English attack in 1589.</p>
          <p>The city is known for its <a href="https://www.coruna.gal/tourism/en/what-to-do-in-a-coruna/cuisine">seafood</a>, served in the bars and restaurants around the old town. Summers are mild and rarely very hot, and in July there is daylight until around 10 pm.</p>
          <a href="https://www.coruna.gal/tourism/en" class="more">Visit A Coruña ↗</a>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="row">
        <h2>Getting to A Coruña</h2>
        <div class="wide"><TravelOptions options={toCity} /></div>
      </section>

      <section class="row">
        <h2>Venue</h2>
        <div class="wide">
          <p>Faculty of Computer Science, Universidade da Coruña</p>
          <iframe
            class="map"
            title="Map of the Faculty of Computer Science, Universidade da Coruña"
            src={`https://www.google.com/maps?q=${place}&z=16&output=embed`}
            loading="lazy"
            referrerpolicy="no-referrer-when-downgrade"
          ></iframe>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="row">
        <h2>Getting to the venue</h2>
        <div class="wide"><TravelOptions options={toCampus} /></div>
      </section>

      {tba.map(t => (
        <section class="row">
          <h2>{t}</h2>
          <span class="status">TBA</span>
        </section>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .wide {
    grid-column: 2 / -1;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .map {
    width: 100%;
    aspect-ratio: 16 / 9;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 4px;
  }

  .wide p a {
    color: var(--ink);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-decoration-color: var(--line);
    text-underline-offset: .2em;
    transition: color .2s ease, text-decoration-color .2s ease;
  }

  .wide p a:hover { color: var(--accent); text-decoration-color: currentColor; }

  .more {
    align-self: flex-start;
    font-size: .9rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    transition: color .2s ease;
  }

  .more:hover { color: var(--accent); }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .wide { grid-column: 1 / -1; }
    .map { aspect-ratio: 4 / 3; }
  }
</style>
